Module eelbell "The Eel Bell" {
  Description "Quillet on the Iscoed sea-bank: a staithe, a church green with a founding-pit, the weirs, the Warden's gate, and three days before the Silver Run.".

  Place washes "the Quillet washes" is region within imbar.
  Place quillet "Quillet" is settlement within washes at 0, 0.
  Place weirs_land "the weirs" is wilderness within washes at 1, 0.
  Place ridge_land "the charcoal ridge" is wilderness within washes at 0, 1.
  Place gate_site "the Warden's gate" is site within washes at 1, 1.
  Place inn "the Two Weirs" is building within quillet.

  Place road "the sea-bank road" is room within quillet at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place staithe "the staithe" is room within quillet at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place green "the church green" is room within quillet at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place taproom "the taproom of the Two Weirs" is room within inn at 1, 1.
  Place cottage "Maudlin Greave's cottage" is room within quillet at 1, 1.
  Place weirs "the eel-weirs" is room within weirs_land at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place clearing "the charcoal clamp" is room within ridge_land at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place gate_foot "the foot of the sea-gate tower" is room within gate_site at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place loft "the bell loft" is room within gate_site at 1, 0.

  Passage bank_way "the sea-bank road" is road between road and staithe taking 10 minutes.
  Passage green_way "the lane to the church green" is path between staithe and green taking 10 minutes.
  Passage inn_door "the Two Weirs' door" is door between staithe and taproom.
  Passage cottage_door "Maudlin Greave's door" is door between staithe and cottage.
  Passage weir_path "the duckboards to the weirs" is path between staithe and weirs taking 10 minutes.
  Passage ridge_path "the track up to the ridge" is track between staithe and clearing taking 30 minutes.
  Passage bank_walk "along the sea-bank to the gate" is path between staithe and gate_foot taking 20 minutes.
  Passage tower_ladder "the tower ladder" is ladder between gate_foot and loft.

  Observe road_scene at road when true "The road is the top of the sea-bank, grass-grown, with the washes on one hand, flat and shining to the edge of the sky, and the sea on the other, which is higher.".
  Observe road_sign at road as sign when not been(party, staithe) "A little way along, a church tower stands with no bell in its louvres, and beyond it the roofs of Quillet, each with a smoke-hole and an eel-net hung to dry.".
  Observe staithe_scene at staithe when true "Eel-boats lie hauled on the hard in rows, black and flat as shoes. Nets hang from every rail, and the whole staithe smells of smoke and mud and something sweet.".
  Observe staithe_gone at staithe as ambience when true "Above the roofs the louvres of the church tower are empty. Nobody looks up at them; everybody has learned not to.".
  Observe green_scene at green when true "The green in front of the bell-less church has been dug into a pit as deep as a man, and a mound of loam stands over it, heaped with goat-hair and horse-dung and old sacking.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low room under smoked rafters, with wooden plates racked on the wall and, on the dresser, a gap where the pewter was.".
  Observe cottage_scene at cottage when true "One room, scrubbed. A man's boots stand by the hearth, greased, as if he were due.".
  Observe weirs_scene at weirs when true "Hurdles of withy run out across the channel in a long V, and in the narrow of it the eel-traps lie stacked like lobster-pots. The water is black and perfectly still.".
  Observe weirs_run at weirs as ambience when true "A boy is mending a trap with his teeth and a knife, looking at the sky.".
  Observe clearing_scene at clearing when true "A mound of turf as big as a cottage smokes quietly on the ridge. It is a clamp: charcoal, under turf, burning without flame, and a man sits by it with a stool and a blanket.".
  Observe gate_scene at gate_foot when true "The Water-Wardens' sea-gate stands in the bank, two great leaves of black oak that have not met in forty years, with the tide-line green up the posts. A squat tower rises beside it, and a lean-to at its foot with a stove.".
  Observe loft_scene at loft when true "A timber frame as wide as a barn door, with nothing hanging in it. Under the louvres a wide, flat shelf of sacking holds the shapes of a bell, in pieces, laid out in order.".

  Thing frame "the empty bell-frame" at loft {
    State empty "Two oak cheeks and a headstock worn with ropes. The frame is empty.".
    State hung "The new bell hangs in the frame, its rope coiled on the floor below.".
  }
}
